## 5. Third-Party Services & External APIs

When using Emaki, the app connects directly from your device to the following services:

| Service | Purpose | Privacy Policy |
|---|---|---|
| **Supabase** | User authentication, cloud vault synchronization, and database hosting | [Supabase Privacy Policy](https://supabase.com/privacy) |
| **Safebooru** | Default family-friendly imageboard feed | [Safebooru Terms](https://safebooru.org) |
| **External / User-Added Boorus** | Content feeds selected or imported by the user (e.g., Danbooru, Gelbooru) | Governed by each individual service's respective policies |

*Note: In the Google Play release flavor of Emaki, all default content is strictly restricted to family-friendly, general-rated imageboards (Safebooru). Users may optionally import external community source configurations, which connect directly from the user's device to those respective endpoints.*

