## 6. Account & Data Deletion Policy

You have full control over your personal data at all times.

### In-App Deletion (Immediate)
You can permanently delete your Emaki account and all associated cloud data directly inside the app:
1. Open **Emaki**.
2. Go to **Profile → Settings (Gear icon)**.
3. Under **Account**, tap **Delete Account & Data**.
4. Confirm the prompt.

**Result:** Your account, profile, cloud vault bookmarks, follows, credentials, and local caches are **immediately, completely, and permanently erased** from our servers and your device.

### Web / Email Deletion Request
If you have uninstalled the app or cannot log in:
- Send an email to **[support@emaki.app](mailto:support@emaki.app)** with the subject `Account Deletion Request - Emaki` and your registered email address.
- Requests are verified and processed within **7 business days** (maximum 30 calendar days).

### Data Retention
Emaki retains **0 days of user data** following account deletion. We do not retain residual copies, archives, or backups of deleted accounts.

